 "caveat": "Feature source: each worm's per-recording summary vector is the single row of the 'features_means' dataset in its Tierpsy/segworm _features.hdf5 file (OWMD, Schafer Lab N2 Bristol single-worm recordings). features_means is a structured array with one row per recording containing ~700 named scalar summary statistics (means over the recording of morphology: length/width/area; posture: bends, eigen_projections, amplitude, wavelength; locomotion: head/midbody/tail speeds, motion direction, crawling/foraging amplitude & frequency, path curvature; and event features: forward/backward/paused fractions, omega/upsilon turns, coils). NO per-frame averaging was performed by this analysis: Tierpsy had already reduced each recording to these summary scalars, so each matrix row is exactly that stored summary vector. Metadata columns worm_index/n_frames/n_valid_skel/first_frame were excluded. Pipeline: union of named features -> drop features NaN/inf in >20% of worms -> median-impute remaining NaN -> drop zero-variance columns -> z-score (per feature) -> PCA via SVD on the z-scored matrix. participation_eff_dim = (sum eig)^2 / sum(eig^2) on covariance eigenvalues; eff_dim_90/99 = #PCs to reach 90%/99% cumulative variance. Each row is one isogenic N2 (Bristol) individual; PCA captures CROSS-INDIVIDUAL behavioural variation among genetically identical worms. Note n_features (~683) >> n_worms (61), so the PCA rank is capped at n_worms-1; the participation ratio and 90/99% dims are the meaningful intrinsic-dimension estimates and are well below that cap.",
 "source": "Zenodo community open-worm-movement-database; query q=N2; files '*_features.hdf5' (Tierpsy/segworm); dataset 'features_means'"
